quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  5,51,"O believers! Do not consider the (hostile) Jews and Christians as (your) guardians (or reliable allies). They are guardians (and supporters) of each other. Anyone of you who trusts them as an ally will (also) become one of them. Indeed, Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people."
  5,52,"You see those with sickness in their hearts rushing towards them, saying: ‘We fear lest fortune may turn against us.’ But perhaps Allah will grant victory or some (other) command (as a sign of success) from Him. Then, they shall be remorseful for what they kept secret in their hearts."
  5,53,"And the believers will say: ‘Are these the ones who swore by Allah their solemn oaths that they were with you?’ All their deeds have gone void, and they have become losers."
  5,54,"O believers! Whoever among you turns away from his faith, Allah will soon bring a people; He shall love them, and they shall love Him. They will be humble towards the believers, firm against the disbelievers, striving hard in Allah’s way and not fearing any blamer’s blame. That is Allah’s grace. He grants it to whomever He pleases. And Allah is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing."
  5,55,"Your only guardians are Allah, His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), and the believers who establish the prayer and give the alms due while bowing down (to Allah)."
  5,56,"Whoever takes as his guardians Allah, His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), and the believers; (these are) Allah’s allies, who will surely be victorious."
  5,57,O believers! Do not take those who ridicule your religion and make fun of it from among those given the Book before you and the disbelievers as (your) trustful allies. And be conscious of Allah if you are (true) believers.
